{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-dd08f32d-3971-43fb-aae1-467fe69de034-10\nfc_389eed04-2367-9d27-bf18-3940ad7230bc_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1 && python3 -c \"\nopen('/tmp/m11-design.md').read()\n\" && sed -n '200,600p' /tmp/m11-design.md","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-dd08f32d-3971-43fb-aae1-467fe69de034-10\nfc_389eed04-2367-9d27-bf18-3940ad7230bc_0","simpleCommands":["cd","python3","sed"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1"}],"fullText":"cd /work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nopen('/tmp/m11-design.md').read()\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nopen('/tmp/m11-design.md').read()\n\""},{"name":"sed","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-n"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'200,600p'"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/m11-design.md"}],"fullText":"sed -n '200,600p' /tmp/m11-design.md"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Print design sections for implementation","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"3b1cca86-e2c4-4155-803f-216a5e66f757","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1 && python3 -c \"\nopen('/tmp/m11-design.md').read()\n\" && sed -n '200,600p' /tmp/m11-design.md","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"| `@group-handle` | Only if no username match: load group by `(workspace_id, handle)`; add each `user_group_members` id that is still a workspace member and ≠ author |\n| `@channel` | All current `channel_members` for the message’s channel except author |\n| `@here` | Intersection of channel members with users that have ≥1 row in `auth_tokens`, except author |\n\n**Invariants:**\n\n- Author id **never** appears in `mentions`.\n- Unknown `@nope` → skip.\n- Mid-word `foo@bar` → no match (unchanged).\n- Soft-deleted / enrich path: recompute from body each read (same as M8 — no stored mentions column).\n\n**mention_count interaction:** when a message is created, for each user id in the resolved `mentions` array, increment that user’s `channel_read_state.mention_count` for this channel (upsert row). **Do not** increment the author’s mention_count. Users not in `mentions` do not get mention bumps (even if `@channel` text appears but resolution excluded them).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; use for badge sync when opening a channel |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz (same as GET messages); return caller’s entry (default zeros if no row) |\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"read_state\": {\n    \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"last_read_seq\": 0,\n    \"unread_count\": 0,\n    \"mention_count\": 0\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf no row exists, return defaults above (do **not** 404). Still 404/403 for channel visibility failures.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n**Body:**\n\n```json\n{ \"last_read_seq\": 42 }\n```\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Send latest observed channel event `seq` from WS (M13) or `0` to acknowledge; while slow keep badges; on 200 replace local badge state from `read_state` |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz; never decrease cursor; update counts; upsert `channel_read_state` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n1. `last_read_seq` required integer, `>= 0`; bool/string → 400.\n2. Load current row (default cursor 0, counts 0).\n3. `new_cursor = max(current.last_read_seq, request.last_read_seq)`.\n4. If request `<` current: **do not** change cursor or counts; return **200** with unchanged entry (idempotent no-op for backwards move).\n5. If advanced:\n   - Set `last_read_seq = new_cursor`, `updated_at=now`.\n   - If `channel_events` / `channel_seq` exist (M13): recompute `unread_count` = count of events with `type='message.created'` and `seq > new_cursor` for this channel; `mention_count` = count of those message.created events whose payload message `mentions` contains caller id (or equivalent join). Cap at non-negative integers.\n   - Else (no M13 tables): set `unread_count=0`, `mention_count=0`.\n6. Return `{ \"read_state\": ReadStateEntry }`.\n\n**Negative:** POST must **not** move `last_read_seq` backwards; must **not** require write membership (read is enough); must **not** work for strangers (404) / private non-members (403).\n\n### Seam: Unread bumps on message create\n\nAfter successful message insert (normal, `/me`, `/shrug`, escaped):\n\nFor every **other** channel member (exclude author):\n\n1. Upsert `channel_read_state` for `(channel_id, member_id)`.\n2. `unread_count += 1`.\n3. If `member_id` ∈ message.mentions: `mention_count += 1`.\n\nAuthor’s row: optionally ensure exists but **do not** bump unread/mention for self.\n\nSide-effect slash commands do **not** bump unread/mention.\n\n### Seam: Workspace detail embed (unchanged shape, live data)\n\n`GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` / join/accept payloads continue to call `list_read_state_for_channels`. After this task, rows are real; shape already correct — **no response schema change**.\n\n### Client slow/fail summary\n\n| Status | Client behavior |\n|--------|-----------------|\n| Search slow | Keep prior results / show loading on search panel |\n| Search 404/401 | Clear results; re-auth on 401 |\n| Slash 201 message null | Update topic/archive UI or member list; no new message row |\n| Slash 400 | Show server message in composer |\n| Read POST fail | Keep prior badges; retry on next focus |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Existing (unchanged DDL)\n\n`channel_read_state(channel_id, user_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count, updated_at)` — PK `(channel_id, user_id)`.\n\n`messages`, `user_groups`, `user_group_members`, `channel_members`, `auth_tokens`, `workspaces`, …\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n**None** in this task (backward compatible). Optional future FTS = separate task after M13 lands.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- `last_read_seq` monotone non-decreasing per `(channel_id, user_id)`.\n- `mention_count` / `unread_count` always ≥ 0.\n- `mentions` array never contains `author_id`.\n- Search never returns `deleted_at IS NOT NULL` rows.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/search/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/search/store.py` | `search_messages(conn, *, workspace_id, user_id, q, limit) -> list[MessageObj]` with visibility SQL |\n| `server/search/routes.py` | `GET /api/search` |\n| `server/messages/slash.py` | Parse + dispatch helpers; command table; escape `//`; pure-ish functions taking conn/channel/caller |\n| `tests/test_search.py` | Search authz, visibility, ordering, empty, validation |\n| `tests/test_slash_commands.py` | All commands, unknown, escape, side-effect shape, authz |\n| `tests/test_mentions_read.py` | `@channel`/`@here`/`@group`, self exclusion, read GET/POST monotonicity, unread bumps |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router(search_router)` |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Intercept slash in `post_channel_message`; add `GET/POST /{channel_id}/read` |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | `get_read_state_entry`, `upsert_advance_read_state`, `bump_unread_for_message`; keep `list_read_state_for_channels` / `READ_STATE_ENTRY_KEYS` |\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Expand `resolve_mentions` (+ channel_id param); call unread bumps from `create_message` (or from route after create); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` |\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Docstring note slash ownership |\n| `tests/test_messages.py` | Update `/shrug hello` expectation to shrugged body (no longer literal `/shrug hello`) |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| Area | Why |\n|------|-----|\n| `static/js/*` | SPA search/badges = MARATHON-17 / follow-up |\n| `server/db.py` migrations | No DDL; M13 owns v6 |\n| Pin / reaction routes | Unchanged |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 |\n| Redis fan-out | MARATHON-14 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (single implementer)\n\n1. `channels/store.py` read helpers + bump helpers.\n2. `messages/store.py` advanced mentions + bump call from create.\n3. `messages/slash.py` + wire into `channels/routes.py` POST messages.\n4. `GET/POST .../read` routes.\n5. `server/search/*` + mount.\n6. Tests; fix `test_messages.py` shrug assertion.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Search package can be built in parallel with slash parser once mention helper signature is agreed.\n- Read routes depend on store helpers only.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumers |\n|----------|-----------|\n| `GET /api/search` → `{messages}` | Future SPA / graders |\n| Slash side-effect **201** `{message:null, channel, invited_user}` | MARATHON-17 composer |\n| Advanced `mentions[]` | SPA highlight; mention_count; M13 payloads |\n| `GET/POST .../read` + live `read_state` rows | Workspace shell badges (M16 already embeds); M17 |\n\n### Upstream\n\n| Dependency | Status |\n|------------|--------|\n| MARATHON-8 messages | Shipped |\n| MARATHON-7 topic/archive helpers | Shipped |\n| MARATHON-12 groups | Shipped |\n| MARATHON-5 read_state shape | Shipped |\n| MARATHON-13 channel_seq/events | Design in review — **soft** dependency for mid-cursor recompute only |\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Dedicated `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` REST (exists in some worktrees / MARATHON-18 notes) — share `add_channel_member` with `/invite` when that route merges; **this task can implement invite via store only**.\n- SPA search panel / unread badges UI.\n- FTS5 performance migration.\n- Presence service replacing auth_token `@here` proxy.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| SPA search UI / composer slash UX | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Frontend task; this is backend-labeled |\n| WS live badge push on unread bump | `server/events.py`, MARATHON-13/14 | Read APIs are pull; fan-out separate |\n| `channel_seq` / `channel_events` DDL | `server/db.py` v6 | MARATHON-13 owns dense seq |\n| File content / filename search | MARATHON-10 files | Only message `body` search here |\n| IRC `/` commands | MARATHON-15 | Different transport |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` public REST | `frontend-dev` neighborhood hit | Not in this task text; `/invite` uses store; REST add-member remains optional follow-up (M18 notes) |\n| Changing pin/reaction semantics | `server/messages/routes.py` | Unrelated |\n| Profile presence / last_active column | — | No presence schema; `@here` uses auth_tokens proxy |\n\nNeighborhood scan accounted for: `test_messages.py` literal `/shrug` (in scope update); `list_read_state_for_channels` / workspace embed (consume, no shape change); `resolve_mentions` username-only (in scope extend); `events.py` no-op publish (call sites only); groups `get_group_by_handle` (consume); archive/topic routes (reuse from slash); no existing `server/search/`.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| `GET /api/search` missing `q` or whitespace-only | **400** `validation_error` |\n| `q` longer than 200 | **400** |\n| Search as non-member of workspace | **404** |\n| Private channel message; caller not member | Omitted from results (not 403 on whole search) |\n| Soft-deleted message matched body historically | Excluded |\n| `/unknown` | **400**; no message row |\n| `/me` / `/me   ` | **400** |\n| `/shrug` no args | **201** message body `¯\\_(ツ)_/¯` |\n| `//archive` | **201** normal message body `/archive` (no side effect) |\n| `/archive` by admin non-owner | **403** |\n| `/archive` already archived | Idempotent store update; **201** `message:null` + channel (`is_archived:true`) |\n| `/invite @missing` | **400** user not found |\n| `/invite @user` already member | **201** idempotent; still return `invited_user` |\n| `/invite` on DM | **403** |\n| `/topic` on archived | **423** |\n| `@channel` in DM | Expands to DM members except author (usually 1 peer) |\n| Author writes `@authorname` | Not in `mentions`; no self mention_count |\n| `@channel` and `@alice` overlapping | Dedupe ids |\n| Username `channel` exists + text `@channel` | Treated as **broadcast**, not that user |\n| Group handle equals a username | Username wins |\n| POST read `last_read_seq` < current | **200** unchanged entry |\n| POST read `last_read_seq` > head_seq | Allowed; store value; counts → 0 (nothing after cursor) |\n| Concurrent bumps | Single SQLite txn per request; accept lost-update rarity under busy_timeout |\n| PATCH message changing mentions | Re-resolve mentions for response; **do not** retroactively rewrite historical mention_count (counts are live counters, not audit) — document: only **create** bumps counts |\n| Empty channel GET read | Defaults zeros |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /api/search?q=hello&workspace_id=<id>` as member → **200** `{messages:[...]}` only from visible channels; substring match case-insensitive; newest-first; exact `MessageObj` keys.\n2. Search without auth → **401**; bad/missing `q` or `workspace_id` → **400**; non-member workspace → **404**.\n3. **Negative:** search must **not** return deleted messages or other-workspace messages.\n4. `POST .../messages` `{body:\"/shrug hi\"}` → **201** body equals `hi ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯` (not literal `/shrug hi`).\n5. `POST` `{body:\"/me dances\"}` → **201** body `_{display_name} dances_`; `{body:\"/me\"}` → **400**.\n6. `POST` `{body:\"//me x\"}` → **201** body `/me x` (literal message).\n7. `POST` `{body:\"/nosuch\"}` → **400**; no new message.\n8. `POST` `{body:\"/topic hello\"}` → **201** `{message:null, channel:{... topic:hello ...}, invited_user:null}`; channel topic persisted; no message row.\n9. `POST` `{body:\"/invite @alice\"}` as permitted caller → **201** `message:null` + `invited_user` UserObj; alice in channel members; DM → **403**.\n10. `POST` `{body:\"/archive\"}` as owner → **201** `message:null` + archived channel; non-owner → **403**.\n11. Message `hello @alice @channel` → `mentions` contains alice and other channel members, **not** author; alice `mention_count` increments; author mention_count does not.\n12. `@here` includes only channel members with auth tokens (except author).\n13. `@grouphandle` expands group members when no user has that username.\n14. `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` → **200** `{read_state: ReadStateEntry}` with all four keys.\n15. `POST /api/channels/{id}/read` `{last_read_seq:N}` never decreases stored cursor; advancing clears or recomputes counts per rules; workspace detail `read_state` entries remain same shape.\n16. **Negative:** must **not** add `seq` to `MessageObj`; must **not** invent new migration conflicting with M13 v6; must **not** implement SPA; must **not** interpret slash on PATCH.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- `tests/test_search.py` — happy path, authz, visibility (private/DM), deleted exclusion, limit bounds, validation.\n- `tests/test_slash_commands.py` — each command; escape; unknown; `/me` empty; side-effect JSON keys; archive authz; invite idempotency; archived topic 423; parent_id on side-effect 400.\n- `tests/test_mentions_read.py` — `@channel`/`@here`/`@group`/self; unread bump; GET defaults; POST monotonicity; workspace detail reflects counts.\n- Update `tests/test_messages.py` shrug assertion.\n- Keep existing suite green (pins, workspaces read_state shape, groups).\n\n### Manual / human\n\n1. Register two users; create workspace; post messages; `curl` search with bearer.\n2. Post `/topic`, `/invite`, `/archive` and confirm `message` is null and channel state changed.\n3. Post `@channel` from user A; as user B `GET .../read` shows mention_count ≥ 1; `POST` read with high seq clears badges.\n4. Confirm `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` `read_state` entries include non-zero counts after unread posts.","stderr":"","executionTime":79,"interleavedOutput":"| `@group-handle` | Only if no username match: load group by `(workspace_id, handle)`; add each `user_group_members` id that is still a workspace member and ≠ author |\n| `@channel` | All current `channel_members` for the message’s channel except author |\n| `@here` | Intersection of channel members with users that have ≥1 row in `auth_tokens`, except author |\n\n**Invariants:**\n\n- Author id **never** appears in `mentions`.\n- Unknown `@nope` → skip.\n- Mid-word `foo@bar` → no match (unchanged).\n- Soft-deleted / enrich path: recompute from body each read (same as M8 — no stored mentions column).\n\n**mention_count interaction:** when a message is created, for each user id in the resolved `mentions` array, increment that user’s `channel_read_state.mention_count` for this channel (upsert row). **Do not** increment the author’s mention_count. Users not in `mentions` do not get mention bumps (even if `@channel` text appears but resolution excluded them).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; use for badge sync when opening a channel |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz (same as GET messages); return caller’s entry (default zeros if no row) |\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"read_state\": {\n    \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"last_read_seq\": 0,\n    \"unread_count\": 0,\n    \"mention_count\": 0\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf no row exists, return defaults above (do **not** 404). Still 404/403 for channel visibility failures.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n**Body:**\n\n```json\n{ \"last_read_seq\": 42 }\n```\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Send latest observed channel event `seq` from WS (M13) or `0` to acknowledge; while slow keep badges; on 200 replace local badge state from `read_state` |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz; never decrease cursor; update counts; upsert `channel_read_state` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n1. `last_read_seq` required integer, `>= 0`; bool/string → 400.\n2. Load current row (default cursor 0, counts 0).\n3. `new_cursor = max(current.last_read_seq, request.last_read_seq)`.\n4. If request `<` current: **do not** change cursor or counts; return **200** with unchanged entry (idempotent no-op for backwards move).\n5. If advanced:\n   - Set `last_read_seq = new_cursor`, `updated_at=now`.\n   - If `channel_events` / `channel_seq` exist (M13): recompute `unread_count` = count of events with `type='message.created'` and `seq > new_cursor` for this channel; `mention_count` = count of those message.created events whose payload message `mentions` contains caller id (or equivalent join). Cap at non-negative integers.\n   - Else (no M13 tables): set `unread_count=0`, `mention_count=0`.\n6. Return `{ \"read_state\": ReadStateEntry }`.\n\n**Negative:** POST must **not** move `last_read_seq` backwards; must **not** require write membership (read is enough); must **not** work for strangers (404) / private non-members (403).\n\n### Seam: Unread bumps on message create\n\nAfter successful message insert (normal, `/me`, `/shrug`, escaped):\n\nFor every **other** channel member (exclude author):\n\n1. Upsert `channel_read_state` for `(channel_id, member_id)`.\n2. `unread_count += 1`.\n3. If `member_id` ∈ message.mentions: `mention_count += 1`.\n\nAuthor’s row: optionally ensure exists but **do not** bump unread/mention for self.\n\nSide-effect slash commands do **not** bump unread/mention.\n\n### Seam: Workspace detail embed (unchanged shape, live data)\n\n`GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` / join/accept payloads continue to call `list_read_state_for_channels`. After this task, rows are real; shape already correct — **no response schema change**.\n\n### Client slow/fail summary\n\n| Status | Client behavior |\n|--------|-----------------|\n| Search slow | Keep prior results / show loading on search panel |\n| Search 404/401 | Clear results; re-auth on 401 |\n| Slash 201 message null | Update topic/archive UI or member list; no new message row |\n| Slash 400 | Show server message in composer |\n| Read POST fail | Keep prior badges; retry on next focus |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Existing (unchanged DDL)\n\n`channel_read_state(channel_id, user_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count, updated_at)` — PK `(channel_id, user_id)`.\n\n`messages`, `user_groups`, `user_group_members`, `channel_members`, `auth_tokens`, `workspaces`, …\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n**None** in this task (backward compatible). Optional future FTS = separate task after M13 lands.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- `last_read_seq` monotone non-decreasing per `(channel_id, user_id)`.\n- `mention_count` / `unread_count` always ≥ 0.\n- `mentions` array never contains `author_id`.\n- Search never returns `deleted_at IS NOT NULL` rows.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/search/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/search/store.py` | `search_messages(conn, *, workspace_id, user_id, q, limit) -> list[MessageObj]` with visibility SQL |\n| `server/search/routes.py` | `GET /api/search` |\n| `server/messages/slash.py` | Parse + dispatch helpers; command table; escape `//`; pure-ish functions taking conn/channel/caller |\n| `tests/test_search.py` | Search authz, visibility, ordering, empty, validation |\n| `tests/test_slash_commands.py` | All commands, unknown, escape, side-effect shape, authz |\n| `tests/test_mentions_read.py` | `@channel`/`@here`/`@group`, self exclusion, read GET/POST monotonicity, unread bumps |