/topic routes (reuse from slash); no existing `server/search/`.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| `GET /api/search` missing `q` or whitespace-only | **400** `validation_error` |\n| `q` longer than 200 | **400** |\n| Search as non-member of workspace | **404** |\n| Private channel message; caller not member | Omitted from results (not 403 on whole search) |\n| Soft-deleted message matched body historically | Excluded |\n| `/unknown` | **400**; no message row |\n| `/me` / `/me   ` | **400** |\n| `/shrug` no args | **201** message body `¯\\_(ツ)_/¯` |\n| `//archive` | **201** normal message body `/archive` (no side effect) |\n| `/archive` by admin non-owner | **403** |\n| `/archive` already archived | Idempotent store update; **201** `message:null` + channel (`is_archived:true`) |\n| `/invite @missing` | **400** user not found |\n| `/invite @user` already member | **201** idempotent; still return `invited_user` |\n| `/invite` on DM | **403** |\n| `/topic` on archived | **423** |\n| `@channel` in DM | Expands to DM members except author (usually 1 peer) |\n| Author writes `@authorname` | Not in `mentions`; no self mention_count |\n| `@channel` and `@alice` overlapping | Dedupe ids |\n| Username `channel` exists + text `@channel` | Treated as **broadcast**, not that user |\n| Group handle equals a username | Username wins |\n| POST read `last_read_seq` < current | **200** unchanged entry |\n| POST read `last_read_seq` > head_seq | Allowed; store value; counts → 0 (nothing after cursor) |\n| Concurrent bumps | Single SQLite txn per request; accept lost-update rarity under busy_timeout |\n| PATCH message changing mentions | Re-resolve mentions for response; **do not** retroactively rewrite historical mention_count (counts are live counters, not audit) — document: only **create** bumps counts |\n| Empty channel GET read | Defaults zeros |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /api/search?q=hello&workspace_id=<id>` as member → **200** `{messages:[...]}` only from visible channels; substring match case-insensitive; newest-first; exact `MessageObj` keys.\n2. Search without auth → **401**; bad/missing `q` or `workspace_id` → **400**; non-member workspace → **404**.\n3. **Negative:** search must **not** return deleted messages or other-workspace messages.\n4. `POST .../messages` `{body:\"/shrug hi\"}` → **201** body equals `hi ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯` (not literal `/shrug hi`).\n5. `POST` `{body:\"/me dances\"}` → **201** body `_{display_name} dances_`; `{body:\"/me\"}` → **400**.\n6. `POST` `{body:\"//me x\"}` → **201** body `/me x` (literal message).\n7. `POST` `{body:\"/nosuch\"}` → **400**; no new message.\n8. `POST` `{body:\"/topic hello\"}` → **201** `{message:null, channel:{... topic:hello ...}, invited_user:null}`; channel topic persisted; no message row.\n9. `POST` `{body:\"/invite @alice\"}` as permitted caller → **201** `message:null` + `invited_user` UserObj; alice in channel members; DM → **403**.\n10. `POST` `{body:\"/archive\"}` as owner → **201** `message:null` + archived channel; non-owner → **403**.\n11. Message `hello @alice @channel` → `mentions` contains alice and other channel members, **not** author; alice `mention_count` increments; author mention_count does not.\n12. `@here` includes only channel members with auth tokens (except author).\n13. `@grouphandle` expands group members when no user has that username.\n14. `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` → **200** `{read_state: ReadStateEntry}` with all four keys.\n15. `POST /api/channels/{id}/read` `{last_read_seq:N}` never decreases stored cursor; advancing clears or recomputes counts per rules; workspace detail `read_state` entries remain same shape.\n16. **Negative:** must **not** add `seq` to `MessageObj`; must **not** invent new migration conflicting with M13 v6; must **not** implement SPA; must **not** interpret slash on PATCH.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- `tests/test_search.py` — happy path, authz, visibility (private/DM), deleted exclusion, limit bounds, validation.\n- `tests/test_slash_commands.py` — each command; escape; unknown; `/me` empty; side-effect JSON keys; archive authz; invite idempotency; archived topic 423; parent_id on side-effect 400.\n- `tests/test_mentions_read.py` — `@channel`/`@here`/`@group`/self; unread bump; GET defaults; POST monotonicity; workspace detail reflects counts.\n- Update `tests/test_messages.py` shrug assertion.\n- Keep existing suite green (pins, workspaces read_state shape, groups).\n\n### Manual / human\n\n1. Register two users; create workspace; post messages; `curl` search with bearer.\n2. Post `/topic`, `/invite`, `/archive` and confirm `message` is null and channel state changed.\n3. Post `@channel` from user A; as user B `GET .../read` shows mention_count ≥ 1; `POST` read with high seq clears badges.\n4. Confirm `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` `read_state` entries include non-zero counts after unread posts.","localExecutionTimeMs":36},"isBackground":false},"description":"Print design sections for implementation"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-dd08f32d-3971-43fb-aae1-467fe69de034-10\nfc_389eed04-2367-9d27-bf18-3940ad7230bc_0","startedAtMs":"1787448794957","completedAtMs":"1787448795036"},"model_call_id":"3bd2270e-ce83-412d-96ec-753a4a8b6e30-3-xt6v","session_id":"3b1cca86-e2c4-4155-803f-216a5e66f757","timestamp_ms":1787448795087}
