{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-3a6c065a-1491-4b6d-9762-adf16cd4eba1-16\nfc_2d7e7c22-ce88-9d58-a62a-e18e0cfb4095_1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1/tests/test_messages.py","limit":120},"result":{"success":{"content":"\"\"\"Contract tests for messages, threads, and reactions (MARATHON-8).\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n\nfrom server.app import create_app\nfrom server.auth.users import USER_OBJ_KEYS\nfrom server.db import (\n    apply_migrations,\n    connect_and_bootstrap,\n    reverse_migration,\n    utc_now_z,\n)\nfrom server.messages.store import MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS\nfrom server.settings import Settings\n\nUSER_KEYS = set(USER_OBJ_KEYS)\nMSG_KEYS = set(MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS)\n\n\ndef _settings(tmp_path: Path, node_id: int = 0) -> Settings:\n    return Settings(\n        node_id=node_id,\n        port=8000 + node_id,\n        data_dir=str(tmp_path),\n        redis_url=\"redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0\",\n    )\n\n\ndef _client(tmp_path: Path, node_id: int = 0) -> TestClient:\n    return TestClient(create_app(_settings(tmp_path, node_id)))\n\n\ndef _register(client: TestClient, username: str) -> dict:\n    resp = client.post(\n        \"/api/auth/register\",\n        json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"password1\"},\n    )\n    assert resp.status_code == 201, resp.text\n    return resp.json()\n\n\ndef _auth(token: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    return {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n\n\ndef _create_ws(client: TestClient, token: str, slug: str = \"acme\") -> dict:\n    resp = client.post(\n        \"/api/workspaces\",\n        headers=_auth(token),\n        json={\"slug\": slug, \"name\": \"Acme\"},\n    )\n    assert resp.status_code == 201, resp.text\n    return resp.json()[\"workspace\"]\n\n\ndef _seed_ws_member(\n    tmp_path: Path, *, workspace_id: str, user_id: str, role: str = \"member\"\n) -> None:\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(str(tmp_path / \"huddle.sqlite\"))\n    try:\n        conn.execute(\n            \"\"\"\n            INSERT INTO workspace_members (workspace_id, user_id, role, created_at)\n            VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\n            \"\"\",\n            (workspace_id, user_id, role, utc_now_z()),\n        )\n        conn.commit()\n    finally:\n        conn.close()\n\n\ndef _setup(tmp_path: Path) -> dict:\n    client = _client(tmp_path)\n    owner = _register(client, \"owner1\")\n    member = _register(client, \"member1\")\n    stranger = _register(client, \"stranger1\")\n    ws = _create_ws(client, owner[\"token\"])\n    _seed_ws_member(\n        tmp_path, workspace_id=ws[\"id\"], user_id=member[\"user\"][\"id\"]\n    )\n    created = client.post(\n        \"/api/workspaces/acme/channels\",\n        headers=_auth(owner[\"token\"]),\n        json={\"name\": \"eng\"},\n    )\n    assert created.status_code == 201, created.text\n    channel = created.json()[\"channel\"]\n    joined = client.post(\n        f\"/api/channels/{channel['id']}/join\",\n        headers=_auth(member[\"token\"]),\n    )\n    assert joined.status_code == 200, joined.text\n    return {\n        \"client\": client,\n        \"owner\": owner,\n        \"member\": member,\n        \"stranger\": stranger,\n        \"ws\": ws,\n        \"channel\": channel,\n    }\n\n\ndef _assert_message_obj(msg: dict) -> None:\n    assert set(msg.keys()) == MSG_KEYS\n    assert set(msg[\"author\"].keys()) == USER_KEYS\n    assert \"seq\" not in msg\n    assert \"blocks\" not in msg\n    assert \"deleted_at\" not in msg\n\n\ndef test_create_list_pagination_and_keys(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    ctx = _setup(tmp_path)","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":624,"fileSize":18418,"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1/tests/test_messages.py","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":120},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-3a6c065a-1491-4b6d-9762-adf16cd4eba1-16\nfc_2d7e7c22-ce88-9d58-a62a-e18e0cfb4095_1","startedAtMs":"1787448799468","completedAtMs":"1787448799521"},"model_call_id":"3bd2270e-ce83-412d-96ec-753a4a8b6e30-4-gazw","session_id":"3b1cca86-e2c4-4155-803f-216a5e66f757","timestamp_ms":1787448799542}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-3a6c065a-1491-4b6d-9762-adf16cd4eba1-15\nfc_2d7e7c22-ce88-9d58-a62a-e18e0cfb4095_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"sed -n '80,280p' /tmp/m11-design.md","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-3a6c065a-1491-4b6d-9762-adf16cd4eba1-15\nfc_2d7e7c22-ce88-9d58-a62a-e18e0cfb4095_0","simpleCommands":["sed"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"sed","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-n"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'80,280p'"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/m11-design.md"}],"fullText":"sed -n '80,280p' /tmp/m11-design.md"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Read slash command design section","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"3b1cca86-e2c4-4155-803f-216a5e66f757","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"sed -n '80,280p' /tmp/m11-design.md","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"|-------|------|--------|\n| `channel_id` | string | Channel UUID |\n| `last_read_seq` | integer ≥ 0 | Dense event seq cursor; default 0; **never decreases** via API |\n| `unread_count` | integer ≥ 0 | Never JSON null |\n| `mention_count` | integer ≥ 0 | Never JSON null; **never** incremented for the message author (no self mention_count) |\n\nExact keys = `READ_STATE_ENTRY_KEYS` already in `server/channels/store.py`.\n\n#### Error codes (this task)\n\n| code | HTTP | When |\n|------|------|------|\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Missing/empty `q` or `workspace_id`; unknown slash command; `/me` without text; malformed `/invite` / `/topic`; invalid `last_read_seq`; invalid limit |\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Slash archive by non-owner; invite without permission; private channel access denied patterns from M7/M8 |\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/workspace; stranger visibility (same matrix as message read) |\n| `archived` | 423 | Message-producing slash or topic change on archived channel (reuse `assert_channel_writable`) |\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=&limit=`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (future SPA)** | Bearer; debounce query; while slow keep prior results; on 200 render `messages`; on 400 show validation; on 404 treat workspace inaccessible |\n| **Server** | Require workspace membership; search visible channels only; return enriched `MessageObj[]` |\n\n**Query params:**\n\n| Param | Required | Rules |\n|-------|----------|--------|\n| `q` | yes | Non-empty after strip; max 200 code points; else 400 |\n| `workspace_id` | yes | UUID string of a workspace the caller belongs to; unknown/non-member → **404** `not_found` (do not leak existence) |\n| `limit` | no | Default **25**; allowed 1..100; invalid → 400 |\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"messages\": [ /* MessageObj, ... */ ]\n}\n```\n\n**Search rules:**\n\n- Match `LOWER(body) LIKE '%' || LOWER(q) || '%'` on non-deleted messages (`deleted_at IS NULL`).\n- Include top-level and thread replies.\n- Channel visibility = same as message **read** (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\n- Order: `created_at DESC`, `id DESC`.\n- Each hit fully enriched via existing `enrich_message_obj` (author, reactions, mentions, files, reply_count).\n- Empty match → `{\"messages\":[]}`.\n\n**Negative:** must **not** return messages from other workspaces; must **not** return soft-deleted bodies; must **not** require channel_id filter.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages` (slash interception)\n\nSame authz as MARATHON-8 message write (channel member + writable). Request body unchanged: `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`.\n\n**Detection order (after authz, before insert):**\n\n1. If `body` (raw string before strip? — use **validated** body string after `validate_message_body` strip rules **except** slash paths may need leading `/`):  \n   **Implement as:** run slash detect on the string after applying the same trim used today **only if** the trimmed string does not start with `/`; if trimmed starts with `/`, parse commands on the trimmed string. Empty after trim still 400.\n2. If trimmed body starts with `//` → **escape**: set effective body to trimmed[1:] (drop one `/`), then normal `create_message` path (mentions, etc.). Example: `//me hi` → stored body `/me hi`.\n3. If trimmed body matches `^/([a-z]+)([\\s\\S]*)$` (command name lowercase letters only):\n   - Known command → dispatch below.\n   - Unknown command name → **400** `validation_error` (`unknown command` / similar); **no** insert.\n4. Else → normal create_message (existing).\n\n**`parent_id` / `file_ids` / `blocks` on side-effect commands:** ignore file/blocks for side effects; if `parent_id` set on side-effect slash → **400** (side effects are channel-level, not thread). Message-producing `/me` and `/shrug` **may** take `parent_id` like normal posts. Escape `//` may take `parent_id`.\n\n#### Message-producing commands → **201** `{ \"message\": MessageObj }`\n\n| Command | Args | Stored `body` | Notes |\n|---------|------|---------------|--------|\n| `/me` | remainder after `/me` trimmed of leading spaces | `_{display_name} {text}_` where `display_name` is author’s current `display_name` and `text` is non-empty remainder | No text / whitespace-only → **400**. Mentions resolved on **stored** body |\n| `/shrug` | optional text | If text empty: `¯\\_(ツ)_/¯`; else `{text} ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯` (single space before shrug) | Always creates message |\n\nAfter create: same unread/mention bumps as normal messages; `publish_message_created`.\n\n#### Side-effect commands → **201** with `message: null`\n\nCommon response base:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": null,\n  \"channel\": null,\n  \"invited_user\": null\n}\n```\n\nOmit keys that are null? **No** — always include all three keys for side-effect responses so clients can branch stably. Message-producing and normal posts keep today’s shape `{ \"message\": MessageObj }` **without** requiring `channel`/`invited_user` keys (backward compatible with MARATHON-8).\n\n| Command | Behavior | Response fields | Authz |\n|---------|----------|-----------------|-------|\n| `/topic` | Remainder (may be empty string) → `channels_store.update_topic` | `channel`=updated `ChannelObj`; `invited_user`=null | Same as PATCH topic; archived → 423 |\n| `/invite` | Require exactly one `@username` token in args (optional extra whitespace). Resolve user; must be workspace member; `add_channel_member` idempotent | `invited_user`=`UserObj`; `channel`=current `ChannelObj` | Caller: workspace owner/admin **or** (channel member and role ∈ {owner,admin,member}); **guest → 403**; **DM → 403**; target not in workspace → 400 |\n| `/archive` | `set_archived(true)` | `channel` updated; `invited_user`=null | Workspace **owner** only (same as POST archive); non-owner → 403; non-member → 404 |\n| `/unarchive` | `set_archived(false)` | same | same as archive |\n\n**`/topic` with no args:** set topic to `\"\"` (allowed by `validate_topic`).\n\n**`/invite` malformed** (no `@user`, multiple `@users`, bare username without `@`) → 400.\n\n**Unknown** e.g. `/foo` → 400.\n\n**Client slow/fail:** while in flight disable send; on 201 if `message===null` refresh channel header/members from `channel`/`invited_user` and do **not** append a bubble; on 400 show `error.message` in composer; on 423 lock composer.\n\n### Seam: Mentions (server-owned resolution)\n\nApplied on create and on PATCH body (re-resolve), including `/me`/`/shrug` stored bodies and `//` escaped bodies.\n\n**Tokenization:** extend scanning beyond today’s username-only regex:\n\n1. Match `@channel` and `@here` as whole tokens with the same word-boundary rules as usernames (`(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])@(channel|here)(?![A-Za-z0-9_])`).\n2. Match `@([a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{1,31})` for user/group (existing charset).\n\n**Resolution → user id list (deduped, stable order = first appearance expansion order):**\n\n| Token | Expansion |\n|-------|-----------|\n| `@username` | If user exists **and** is workspace member **and** id ≠ author → that id. Else skip (not 400) |\n| `@group-handle` | Only if no username match: load group by `(workspace_id, handle)`; add each `user_group_members` id that is still a workspace member and ≠ author |\n| `@channel` | All current `channel_members` for the message’s channel except author |\n| `@here` | Intersection of channel members with users that have ≥1 row in `auth_tokens`, except author |\n\n**Invariants:**\n\n- Author id **never** appears in `mentions`.\n- Unknown `@nope` → skip.\n- Mid-word `foo@bar` → no match (unchanged).\n- Soft-deleted / enrich path: recompute from body each read (same as M8 — no stored mentions column).\n\n**mention_count interaction:** when a message is created, for each user id in the resolved `mentions` array, increment that user’s `channel_read_state.mention_count` for this channel (upsert row). **Do not** increment the author’s mention_count. Users not in `mentions` do not get mention bumps (even if `@channel` text appears but resolution excluded them).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; use for badge sync when opening a channel |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz (same as GET messages); return caller’s entry (default zeros if no row) |\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"read_state\": {\n    \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"last_read_seq\": 0,\n    \"unread_count\": 0,\n    \"mention_count\": 0\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf no row exists, return defaults above (do **not** 404). Still 404/403 for channel visibility failures.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n**Body:**\n\n```json\n{ \"last_read_seq\": 42 }\n```\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Send latest observed channel event `seq` from WS (M13) or `0` to acknowledge; while slow keep badges; on 200 replace local badge state from `read_state` |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz; never decrease cursor; update counts; upsert `channel_read_state` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n1. `last_read_seq` required integer, `>= 0`; bool/string → 400.\n2. Load current row (default cursor 0, counts 0).\n3. `new_cursor = max(current.last_read_seq, request.last_read_seq)`.\n4. If request `<` current: **do not** change cursor or counts; return **200** with unchanged entry (idempotent no-op for backwards move).\n5. If advanced:\n   - Set `last_read_seq = new_cursor`, `updated_at=now`.\n   - If `channel_events` / `channel_seq` exist (M13): recompute `unread_count` = count of events with `type='message.created'` and `seq > new_cursor` for this channel; `mention_count` = count of those message.created events whose payload message `mentions` contains caller id (or equivalent join). Cap at non-negative integers.\n   - Else (no M13 tables): set `unread_count=0`, `mention_count=0`.\n6. Return `{ \"read_state\": ReadStateEntry }`.\n\n**Negative:** POST must **not** move `last_read_seq` backwards; must **not** require write membership (read is enough); must **not** work for strangers (404) / private non-members (403).\n\n### Seam: Unread bumps on message create\n\nAfter successful message insert (normal, `/me`, `/shrug`, escaped):\n\nFor every **other** channel member (exclude author):\n\n1. Upsert `channel_read_state` for `(channel_id, member_id)`.\n2. `unread_count += 1`.\n3. If `member_id` ∈ message.mentions: `mention_count += 1`.\n\nAuthor’s row: optionally ensure exists but **do not** bump unread/mention for self.\n\nSide-effect slash commands do **not** bump unread/mention.\n\n### Seam: Workspace detail embed (unchanged shape, live data)\n\n`GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` / join/accept payloads continue to call `list_read_state_for_channels`. After this task, rows are real; shape already correct — **no response schema change**.\n\n### Client slow/fail summary\n","stderr":"","executionTime":69,"interleavedOutput":"|-------|------|--------|\n| `channel_id` | string | Channel UUID |\n| `last_read_seq` | integer ≥ 0 | Dense event seq cursor; default 0; **never decreases** via API |\n| `unread_count` | integer ≥ 0 | Never JSON null |\n| `mention_count` | integer ≥ 0 | Never JSON null; **never** incremented for the message author (no self mention_count) |\n\nExact keys = `READ_STATE_ENTRY_KEYS` already in `server/channels/store.py`.\n\n#### Error codes (this task)\n\n| code | HTTP | When |\n|------|------|------|\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Missing/empty `q` or `workspace_id`; unknown slash command; `/me` without text; malformed `/invite` / `/topic`; invalid `last_read_seq`; invalid limit |\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Slash archive by non-owner; invite without permission; private channel access denied patterns from M7/M8 |\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/workspace; stranger visibility (same matrix as message read) |\n| `archived` | 423 | Message-producing slash or topic change on archived channel (reuse `assert_channel_writable`) |\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=&limit=`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (future SPA)** | Bearer; debounce query; while slow keep prior results; on 200 render `messages`; on 400 show validation; on 404 treat workspace inaccessible |\n| **Server** | Require workspace membership; search visible channels only; return enriched `MessageObj[]` |\n\n**Query params:**\n\n| Param | Required | Rules |\n|-------|----------|--------|\n| `q` | yes | Non-empty after strip; max 200 code points; else 400 |\n| `workspace_id` | yes | UUID string of a workspace the caller belongs to; unknown/non-member → **404** `not_found` (do not leak existence) |\n| `limit` | no | Default **25**; allowed 1..100; invalid → 400 |\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"messages\": [ /* MessageObj, ... */ ]\n}\n```\n\n**Search rules:**\n\n- Match `LOWER(body) LIKE '%' || LOWER(q) || '%'` on non-deleted messages (`deleted_at IS NULL`).\n- Include top-level and thread replies.\n- Channel visibility = same as message **read** (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\n- Order: `created_at DESC`, `id DESC`.\n- Each hit fully enriched via existing `enrich_message_obj` (author, reactions, mentions, files, reply_count).\n- Empty match → `{\"messages\":[]}`.\n\n**Negative:** must **not** return messages from other workspaces; must **not** return soft-deleted bodies; must **not** require channel_id filter.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages` (slash interception)\n\nSame authz as MARATHON-8 message write (channel member + writable). Request body unchanged: `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`.\n\n**Detection order (after authz, before insert):**\n\n1. If `body` (raw string before strip? — use **validated** body string after `validate_message_body` strip rules **except** slash paths may need leading `/`):  \n   **Implement as:** run slash detect on the string after applying the same trim used today **only if** the trimmed string does not start with `/`; if trimmed starts with `/`, parse commands on the trimmed string. Empty after trim still 400.\n2. If trimmed body starts with `//` → **escape**: set effective body to trimmed[1:] (drop one `/`), then normal `create_message` path (mentions, etc.). Example: `//me hi` → stored body `/me hi`.\n3. If trimmed body matches `^/([a-z]+)([\\s\\S]*)$` (command name lowercase letters only):\n   - Known command → dispatch below.\n   - Unknown command name → **400** `validation_error` (`unknown command` / similar); **no** insert.\n4. Else → normal create_message (existing).\n\n**`parent_id` / `file_ids` / `blocks` on side-effect commands:** ignore file/blocks for side effects; if `parent_id` set on side-effect slash → **400** (side effects are channel-level, not thread). Message-producing `/me` and `/shrug` **may** take `parent_id` like normal posts. Escape `//` may take `parent_id`.\n\n#### Message-producing commands → **201** `{ \"message\": MessageObj }`\n\n| Command | Args | Stored `body` | Notes |\n|---------|------|---------------|--------|\n| `/me` | remainder after `/me` trimmed of leading spaces | `_{display_name} {text}_` where `display_name` is author’s current `display_name` and `text` is non-empty remainder | No text / whitespace-only → **400**. Mentions resolved on **stored** body |\n| `/shrug` | optional text | If text empty: `¯\\_(ツ)_/¯`; else `{text} ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯` (single space before shrug) | Always creates message |\n\nAfter create: same unread/mention bumps as normal messages; `publish_message_created`.\n\n#### Side-effect commands → **201** with `message: null`\n\nCommon response base:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": null,\n  \"channel\": null,\n  \"invited_user\": null\n}\n```\n\nOmit keys that are null? **No** — always include all three keys for side-effect responses so clients can branch stably. Message-producing and normal posts keep today’s shape `{ \"message\": MessageObj }` **without** requiring `channel`/`invited_user` keys (backward compatible with MARATHON-8).\n\n| Command | Behavior | Response fields | Authz |\n|---------|----------|-----------------|-------|\n| `/topic` | Remainder (may be empty string) → `channels_store.update_topic` | `channel`=updated `ChannelObj`; `invited_user`=null | Same as PATCH topic; archived → 423 |\n| `/invite` | Require exactly one `@username` token in args (optional extra whitespace). Resolve user; must be workspace member; `add_channel_member` idempotent | `invited_user`=`UserObj`; `channel`=current `ChannelObj` | Caller: workspace owner/admin **or** (channel member and role ∈ {owner,admin,member}); **guest → 403**; **DM → 403**; target not in workspace → 400 |\n| `/archive` | `set_archived(true)` | `channel` updated; `invited_user`=null | Workspace **owner** only (same as POST archive); non-owner → 403; non-member → 404 |\n| `/unarchive` | `set_archived(false)` | same | same as archive |\n\n**`/topic` with no args:** set topic to `\"\"` (allowed by `validate_topic`).\n\n**`/invite` malformed** (no `@user`, multiple `@users`, bare username without `@`) → 400.\n\n**Unknown** e.g. `/foo` → 400.\n\n**Client slow/fail:** while in flight disable send; on 201 if `message===null` refresh channel header/members from `channel`/`invited_user` and do **not** append a bubble; on 400 show `error.message` in composer; on 423 lock composer.\n\n### Seam: Mentions (server-owned resolution)\n\nApplied on create and on PATCH body (re-resolve), including `/me`/`/shrug` stored bodies and `//` escaped bodies.\n\n**Tokenization:** extend scanning beyond today’s username-only regex:\n\n1. Match `@channel` and `@here` as whole tokens with the same word-boundary rules as usernames (`(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])@(channel|here)(?![A-Za-z0-9_])`).\n2. Match `@([a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{1,31})` for user/group (existing charset).\n\n**Resolution → user id list (deduped, stable order = first appearance expansion order):**\n\n| Token | Expansion |\n|-------|-----------|\n| `@username` | If user exists **and** is workspace member **and** id ≠ author → that id. Else skip (not 400) |\n| `@group-handle` | Only if no username match: load group by `(workspace_id, handle)`; add each `user_group_members` id that is still a workspace member and ≠ author |\n| `@channel` | All current `channel_members` for the message’s channel except author |\n| `@here` | Intersection of channel members with users that have ≥1 row in `auth_tokens`, except author |\n\n**Invariants:**\n\n- Author id **never** appears in `mentions`.\n- Unknown `@nope` → skip.\n- Mid-word `foo@bar` → no match (unchanged).\n- Soft-deleted / enrich path: recompute from body each read (same as M8 — no stored mentions column).\n\n**mention_count interaction:** when a message is created, for each user id in the resolved `mentions` array, increment that user’s `channel_read_state.mention_count` for this channel (upsert row). **Do not** increment the author’s mention_count. Users not in `mentions` do not get mention bumps (even if `@channel` text appears but resolution excluded them).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; use for badge sync when opening a channel |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz (same as GET messages); return caller’s entry (default zeros if no row) |\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"read_state\": {\n    \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"last_read_seq\": 0,\n    \"unread_count\": 0,\n    \"mention_count\": 0\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf no row exists, return defaults above (do **not** 404). Still 404/403 for channel visibility failures.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/read`\n\n**Body:**\n\n```json\n{ \"last_read_seq\": 42 }\n```\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Send latest observed channel event `seq` from WS (M13) or `0` to acknowledge; while slow keep badges; on 200 replace local badge state from `read_state` |\n| **Server** | Channel **read** authz; never decrease cursor; update counts; upsert `channel_read_state` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n1. `last_read_seq` required integer, `>= 0`; bool/string → 400.\n2. Load current row (default cursor 0, counts 0).\n3. `new_cursor = max(current.last_read_seq, request.last_read_seq)`.\n4. If request `<` current: **do not** change cursor or counts; return **200** with unchanged entry (idempotent no-op for backwards move).\n5. If advanced:\n   - Set `last_read_seq = new_cursor`, `updated_at=now`.\n   - If `channel_events` / `channel_seq` exist (M13): recompute `unread_count` = count of events with `type='message.created'` and `seq > new_cursor` for this channel; `mention_count` = count of those message.created events whose payload message `mentions` contains caller id (or equivalent join). Cap at non-negative integers.\n   - Else (no M13 tables): set `unread_count=0`, `mention_count=0`.\n6. Return `{ \"read_state\": ReadStateEntry }`.\n\n**Negative:** POST must **not** move `last_read_seq` backwards; must **not** require write membership (read is enough); must **not** work for strangers (404) / private non-members (403).\n\n### Seam: Unread bumps on message create\n\nAfter successful message insert (normal, `/me`, `/shrug`, escaped):\n\nFor every **other** channel member (exclude author):\n\n1. Upsert `channel_read_state` for `(channel_id, member_id)`.\n2. `unread_count += 1`.\n3. If `member_id` ∈ message.mentions: `mention_count += 1`.\n\nAuthor’s row: optionally ensure exists but **do not** bump unread/mention for self.\n\nSide-effect slash commands do **not** bump unread/mention.\n\n### Seam: Workspace detail embed (unchanged shape, live data)\n\n`GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` / join/accept payloads continue to call `list_read_state_for_channels`. After this task, rows are real; shape already correct — **no response schema change**.\n\n### Client slow/fail summary\n","localExecutionTimeMs":24},"isBackground":false},"description":"Read slash command design section"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-3a6c065a-1491-4b6d-9762-adf16cd4eba1-15\nfc_2d7e7c22-ce88-9d58-a62a-e18e0cfb4095_0","startedAtMs":"1787448799468","completedAtMs":"1787448799538"},"model_call_id":"3bd2270e-ce83-412d-96ec-753a4a8b6e30-4-gazw","session_id":"3b1cca86-e2c4-4155-803f-216a5e66f757","timestamp_ms":1787448799561}
